          <h2>Subgrid-Aligned Article Cards</h2>
          <p>
            Uneven card baselines are the most common visual defect on editorial websites. When article titles vary in length, cards become uneven and bottom links misalign across columns.
          </p>
          <p>
            With Kōshi, each card adopts <code>kos-subgrid="rows"</code> and <code>kos-row-span="4"</code>. On desktop, child cards participate directly in the parent grid's shared row tracks so buttons align horizontally. Below <code>48rem</code>, Kōshi gracefully reflows into a single column with safe vertical item spacing:
          </p>

