          <h2>Hakugin-hi (Silver Ratio) & Yohaku (Negative Space)</h2>
          <p>
            In Japanese architecture, space is measured by <em>Tatami</em> modularity and the Silver Ratio (<em>Hakugin-hi</em>, <code>1:1.414</code>). Root-two proportion represents the exact ratio found in international A-series paper formats (A4, A5, A3).
          </p>
          <p>
            By pairing <code>kos-ratio="silver"</code> with <code>kos-offset="1"</code>, we introduce an intentional negative space channel (*yohaku*) that separates portrait photography from longform prose.
          </p>

